<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean Sept C/A deficit rises to $1.41 bln.</title>
<headline>S.Korean Sept C/A deficit rises to $1.41 bln.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's current account deficit soared to $1.41 billion in September from a $753.1 million shortfall a year earlier, preliminary figures from the Bank of Korea (BOK) showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>				 Sept/96	  Aug/96	 Sept/95</p>
<p>    Current account     -1,414.9	-3,524.0	  -753.1</p>
<p>    Trade account	   -812.9	-2,875.2	  -295.9</p>
<p>    Exports (FOB)	 10,086.1	 9,538.4	10,715.9</p>
<p>    Imports (FOB)	 10,899.0	12,413.6	11,011.8</p>
<p>    Invisible trade	 -508.7	  -602.4	  -408.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are in millions of U.S. dollars</p>
</text>
